Chapter: ScenePlaceTest
  cites Works chapter GopScene
  cites Engine chapter Renderer3D
  cites Engine chapter GpuScene
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 A windowed 3D pane is placed again before every frame, and placing it does
 not touch the BUFFERS.

 That is why maximise and restore are affordable for these two panes. The
 colour and depth buffers are allocated once, at the size of the content box,
 which is the largest rectangle a window on this desk can take; `gsc-place`
 rebuilds the render target from them with the window's width and height and
 the buffer's stride. The alternative was a target reallocated on every
 resize, which would leave the old one above the pane's own heap mark until
 the pane closed -- 6.4 measured that tail at about 3 MB stranded per docked
 pane against a 128 MB arena, and a maximise button is a great deal easier to
 press than a pane is to dock.

 IT IS NOT FREE, AND THE FIRST VERSION OF THIS FILE CLAIMED IT WAS. Placing
 builds a `GpuView` and an `R3dTriState` and stores them, and records are
 heap: two placements measured 1,392 bytes. Per frame that is nothing --
 `desk-loop` brackets each iteration and drops it -- but it is not zero, and a
 file asserting zero would have gone red the first time anybody looked.

 So the assertion is the one that matters: what two placements cost, against
 what ONE buffer would cost if the target were rebuilt instead. Those two
 numbers are three orders of magnitude apart at this tiny size and five at a
 real one, which is a comparison rather than a threshold somebody chose.

 THE HEAP PROBE IS `alloc-bytes 0`. It advances the bump allocator by nothing
 and answers the current frontier, so a difference across a call is the bytes
 that call made permanent. A probe that always reads zero is not evidence, so
 the last row allocates a known 64 bytes and the same probe must SEE it; a
 zero there would mean the instrument was never working.

 The fields are asserted against the rect rather than against recorded
 numbers, because a recorded number cannot tell a correct placement from a
 stale one that happens to match at the size every capture is taken at.

 TWO ROWS AND ONLY ONE OF THEM CAN FAIL, WHICH IS THE POINT OF THE SMALL ONE.
 Sabotaged by forcing the target's width back to the buffer's, `small` reads
 `tgt 320x120` and disagrees while `full` still agrees -- at the full content
 box those two numbers ARE equal, so a window the size of the box can never
 see the difference. A file with only the full row would have passed.

Section: Test

  sp-fake : Integer, Integer -> ScenePane
  sp-fake (bw) (bh) =
    let px = alloc-bytes (bw * bh * 4)
    in let dp = alloc-bytes (bw * bh * 4)
    in ScenePane {
      sp-tgt = R3dTriState { r3t-base = px, r3t-depth = dp, r3t-w = bw, r3t-h = bh, r3t-stride = bw },
      sp-px = px,
      sp-dp = dp,
      sp-bw = bw,
      sp-gv = gv-new 0 0 bw bh,
      sp-sky = 0,
      sp-ch = bh,
      sp-fb = 0,
      sp-sh = 1,
      sp-gpu = 0,
      sp-n = 0,
      sp-t0 = 0,
      sp-yaw = 0,
      sp-look = 0,
      sp-ptr = 0
    }

  sp-yn : Boolean -> Text
  sp-yn (v) = if v then "yes" else "no"

  sp-shows : ScenePane, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Text
  sp-shows (sp) (x) (y) (w) (h) =
    let gv = sp.sp-gv
    in let t = sp.sp-tgt
    in "gv " & integer-to-text (gv.gv-x) & "," & integer-to-text (gv.gv-y) & " " & integer-to-text (gv.gv-w) & "x" & integer-to-text (gv.gv-h) & "  tgt " & integer-to-text (t.r3t-w) & "x" & integer-to-text (t.r3t-h) & " stride " & integer-to-text (t.r3t-stride) & "  ch " & integer-to-text (sp.sp-ch)

  sp-agrees : ScenePane, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  sp-agrees (sp) (base) (stride) (x) (y) (w) (h) =
    let gv = sp.sp-gv
    in let t = sp.sp-tgt
    in (gv.gv-x) == x & (gv.gv-y) == y & (gv.gv-w) == w & (gv.gv-h) == h - gsc-label-band
       & (t.r3t-w) == w & (t.r3t-h) == h & (t.r3t-stride) == sp.sp-bw
       & sp.sp-ch == h & sp.sp-fb == base + y * stride * 4
       & (t.r3t-base) == sp.sp-px & (t.r3t-depth) == sp.sp-dp

  opening : [Console] Nothing =
    let sp = sp-fake 320 200
    in let base = 4096
    in let stride = 1600
    in let h0 = alloc-bytes 0
    in let p1 = gsc-place sp base stride 40 60 240 120
    in let ok1 = sp-agrees sp base stride 40 60 240 120
    in let show1 = sp-shows sp 40 60 240 120
    in let p2 = gsc-place sp base stride 0 30 320 200
    in let ok2 = sp-agrees sp base stride 0 30 320 200
    in let show2 = sp-shows sp 0 30 320 200
    in let h1 = alloc-bytes 0
    in let burn = alloc-bytes 64
    in let h2 = alloc-bytes 0
    in act
      print-line-uni ("small   " & show1 & "  agrees " & sp-yn ok1)
      print-line-uni ("full    " & show2 & "  agrees " & sp-yn ok2)
      print-line-uni ("two placements cost " & integer-to-text (h1 - h0) & " bytes, one buffer would cost " & integer-to-text (320 * 200 * 4) & ": cheaper " & sp-yn (h1 - h0 < 320 * 200 * 4))
      print-line-uni ("the probe can see 64: " & sp-yn (h2 - h1 >= 64))
      print-line-uni ("buffers unmoved: " & sp-yn (sp.sp-px /= 0 & sp.sp-bw == 320))
    end

